// worker existed. Only the install roots are precached; every other chunk is kept
// by `cacheFirst` on its first fetch, and a first visit's fetches never reached
// it. The home's weather layer was one: online once, then offline, the reload met
// "Unable to preload CSS" and the whole estate fell to its error panel. The page
// names the hashed chunks it loaded (`ADOPT_CHUNKS`) and they join the shell
// store, where `cacheFirst` looks; the fetch is answered by the HTTP cache.
